I got a bunch of these questions about the
connection, the possible connection between

00:00:11.020 --> 00:00:14.150
Corona virus and the election in November.

00:00:14.150 --> 00:00:15.150
Take a listen.

00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:16.309
[00:48:46][13.8]
[00:48:48] Oh, David.

00:00:16.309 --> 00:00:20.390
The name is Storrar, longtime follower question
for you.

00:00:20.390 --> 00:00:30.230
If the Corona virus should keep going on until
November election time, could a Trump declare

00:00:30.230 --> 00:00:38.730
the election, postpone, cancel and essentially
go on as president without an actual election?

00:00:38.730 --> 00:00:40.160
[00:49:10][22.2]
[00:49:11] Not really.

00:00:40.160 --> 00:00:41.320
So here's the thing.

00:00:41.320 --> 00:00:45.570
First of all, Trump couldn't postpone the
election by himself.

00:00:45.570 --> 00:00:50.320
You would need congressional support to do
it, even with congressional support.

00:00:50.320 --> 00:00:52.440
It would be difficult to do.

00:00:52.440 --> 00:00:58.930
Trump could say it, but that would not make
it so because Congress sets the time, place

00:00:58.930 --> 00:01:01.140
and manner of federal elections.

00:01:01.140 --> 00:01:03.059
But the thing is the following.

00:01:03.059 --> 00:01:10.720
Congress would need to rewrite three U.S.
codes, subsection 7, which has the timeline

00:01:10.720 --> 00:01:15.119
for electors, which are chosen by states to
vote in the Electoral College.

00:01:15.119 --> 00:01:17.180
Remember when we vote in November?

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:22.390
Each state is saying we want our electors
to vote in this way at the nominating convention.

00:01:22.390 --> 00:01:27.400
The electors convention that is set for December
14th.

00:01:27.400 --> 00:01:33.880
So if lawmakers manage to delay the election,
they really couldn't delay it beyond, you

00:01:33.880 --> 00:01:39.119
know, a few days before December 14th without
having to rewrite the Constitution itself,

00:01:39.119 --> 00:01:44.050
which says the president can hold to office
a term of four years.

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:46.689
The election is happening at this place, so
on and so forth.

00:01:46.689 --> 00:01:50.100
Now, here's the other thing that a lot of
people are worried about, which is imagine

00:01:50.100 --> 00:01:52.860
that Trump succeeds in doing it.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.560
Does he just remain president?

00:01:54.560 --> 00:01:59.549
And the answer is no, because this has been
researched.

00:01:59.549 --> 00:02:06.890
The 20th Amendment terminates each presidential
term at noon on January 20.

00:02:06.890 --> 00:02:14.379
So even if at the federal level, at state
level, things were delayed, Trump as president

00:02:14.379 --> 00:02:17.719
would be terminated on January 20th regardless.

00:02:17.719 --> 00:02:20.659
Now, of course, it would all be a legal fight.

00:02:20.659 --> 00:02:23.029
It would be unprecedented territory.

00:02:23.029 --> 00:02:28.510
But the idea that Trump could do this to just
stay in power for some period of time seems

00:02:28.510 --> 00:02:33.489
extraordinarily unlikely and not something
that I would I would put too much time into

00:02:33.489 --> 00:02:34.489
worrying about.

00:02:34.489 --> 00:02:38.400
The real question now is what's going to happen
with the primary Louisiana and Georgia already

00:02:38.400 --> 00:02:40.090
deciding to delay primaries.

00:02:40.090 --> 00:02:44.620
There's now a fight about whether the primaries
happening in March should even be delayed.

00:02:44.620 --> 00:02:47.079
That is a much more present, present thing.

